cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
title: "Tremor Lab: aftershock-sequence statistics in Python"
abstract: >-
  Estimators for aftershock sequences: the magnitude of completeness by maximum
  curvature, the Gutenberg-Richter b-value by the Aki maximum-likelihood estimator with
  the Shi and Bolt standard error, the modified Omori-Utsu decay by maximum likelihood
  with a bootstrap uncertainty, radiated energy and the Bath energy screen, and
  magnitude homogenisation to Mw by the Scordilis relations.
type: software
version: 1.1.0
license: MIT
authors:
  - given-names: Aik
    family-names: Kazarian
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-1842-1590"
    affiliation: "National Academy of Sciences of Armenia"
keywords:
  - seismology
  - aftershocks
  - Gutenberg-Richter
  - b-value
  - Omori-Utsu
repository-code: "https://github.com/HaikKaz/tremor-lab"
